  "narrative": {
    "text": "Figure 2.2. An infographic titled 'REDDHI — Resilient Essential Data & Digital Health Infrastructure', subtitled 'a direction of travel, not a fixed destination or a single system'. Panels explain why 'resilient' (survives funding volatility, reduces vendor dependency, long-term sustainability, local capacity) and why 'essential' (minimum capabilities, a foundation for many use cases, investment efficiency, a subset of the national architecture); the full-STAC foundations (Standards such as HL7 FHIR, ICD, SNOMED CT, LOINC and CQL; open-source Technologies; DPI-based Architectures; WHO SMART Guidelines Content); REDDHI's role in the national architecture; five objectives; and the guiding principles as a set of tags.",
